(5630577, 815299, 19064, '<td valign="top">Stunning, I love it. Reminds me of an album or cd cover</td>', 'Stunning, I love it. Reminds me of an album or cd cover', '2009-09-01 10:58:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5630589, 815912, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for your shot to be critiqued! <br/> <br/>First off, fantastic colours, the warmth and depth of the colour really brings out teh thoughts of crisp mornings, apple pies and warm fires. Your lighting is very good as well. <br/> <br/>I think that the only nitpick that i have is that it is such a powerful image that the bottom being out of focus throws you off.  Would have liked to have seen that as tack sharp as the rest of the shot it. Also the water drop, it neither makes the shot worse or better, it is one of those could be coudnt be there not going to hurt the shot. <br/> <br/>Overall , very pleasing shot, well done</td>', 'Hi from the C Club You asked for your shot to be critiqued!  First off, fantastic colours, the warmth and depth of the colour really brings out teh thoughts of crisp mornings, apple pies and warm fires. Your lighting is very good as well.  I think that the only nitpick that i have is that it is such a powerful image that the bottom being out of focus throws you off.  Would have liked to have seen that as tack sharp as the rest of the shot it. Also the water drop, it neither makes the shot worse or better, it is one of those could be coudnt be there not going to hurt the shot.  Overall , very pleasing shot, well done', '2009-09-01 11:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5630603, 815474, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for your shot to be critiqued! <br/> <br/>I like the vibrancy that you have going on in this shot. Your lighting is pretty harsh in this shot as you can see from the bounce that is going on in there. I think that a closer crop all around to make a sqaure crop would have focused us more on the marco that it is .  The center is a jumble of abstract and should have been concentrated there.<br/> <br/>even though your shot is full of colours it is coming across as fairly flat, I played with it roughly and this is what i got <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=818614" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/818614.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/818614.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/818614.jpg"/></a>  now i used brightness and contrast, selective colours in black only, adn then repeat and flip. I am not saying you have to do this, but it gives you another idea of what could be done iwth your shot to make it more abstract and with a feeling of depth. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club You asked for your shot to be critiqued!  I like the vibrancy that you have going on in this shot. Your lighting is pretty harsh in this shot as you can see from the bounce that is going on in there. I think that a closer crop all around to make a sqaure crop would have focused us more on the marco that it is .  The center is a jumble of abstract and should have been concentrated there. even though your shot is full of colours it is coming across as fairly flat, I played with it roughly and this is what i got   now i used brightness and contrast, selective colours in black only, adn then repeat and flip. I am not saying you have to do this, but it gives you another idea of what could be done iwth your shot to make it more abstract and with a feeling of depth.  ', '2009-09-01 11:21:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5630610, 814806, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>Well, I had no idea as to what it was even with reading you title.  To me it looks like planks of wood, so very well done on this shot!  I have this a fairly high score in the challenge. <br/> <br/>I think it is a great picture, I like the black and white of it, i like your details and sharpness.  I really  don''t think that there is much more you could have done with this shot.  Maybe a little more sharpening to get those amazing grooves really to stand out and a tiny crop of the left hand side to get rid of the blown out white on the prong. Bar that it is a brilliant shot  well done</td>', 'Hi from the C Club Well, I had no idea as to what it was even with reading you title.  To me it looks like planks of wood, so very well done on this shot!  I have this a fairly high score in the challenge.  I think it is a great picture, I like the black and white of it, i like your details and sharpness.  I really  don''t think that there is much more you could have done with this shot.  Maybe a little more sharpening to get those amazing grooves really to stand out and a tiny crop of the left hand side to get rid of the blown out white on the prong. Bar that it is a brilliant shot  well done', '2009-09-01 11:30:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5630753, 816024, 60614, '<td valign="top">Oh my I almost entered a similiar shot.  Mine was a glass decanter with colored marbles in it.  But in the end I entered my crinkled tin foil.  Great minds think a like.  Very nice macro.  Definately deserved a better score.</td>', 'Oh my I almost entered a similiar shot.  Mine was a glass decanter with colored marbles in it.  But in the end I entered my crinkled tin foil.  Great minds think a like.  Very nice macro.  Definately deserved a better score.', '2009-09-01 13:49:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5631373, 815662, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>you asked for your shot in the abstract macro to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First off, great shot.  It isn''t really macro enough to be called a macro though.  Maybe really zooming in on the twisted metal would have achieved this. Also, your first peg is not in alignment with the other pegs and makes the eye go up and down, which does not help the composition.<br/> <br/>Your POV is good, and your DOF is good.  The only thing I would have done differently in this is the crop.  Post processing is great. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club you asked for your shot in the abstract macro to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club. First off, great shot.  It isn''t really macro enough to be called a macro though.  Maybe really zooming in on the twisted metal would have achieved this. Also, your first peg is not in alignment with the other pegs and makes the eye go up and down, which does not help the composition. Your POV is good, and your DOF is good.  The only thing I would have done differently in this is the crop.  Post processing is great.  ', '2009-09-01 20:55:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5631381, 816181, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>Cool shot, it is something completely different than what I thought it was when I was voting. <br/> <br/>The only thing wrong with this shot is the focus and you touched upon that in your comments. I am not sure if unsharp mask could have helped any here, but it is worth a shot. Flipping the shot may have been interesting too.    There really is not a lot I can say about a perfect picture that just needs one thing sorting. <br/> <br/>I love how the smooth curves all compliment each other, the red is very sensual, I could stare at lava lamps for hours. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   Cool shot, it is something completely different than what I thought it was when I was voting.  The only thing wrong with this shot is the focus and you touched upon that in your comments. I am not sure if unsharp mask could have helped any here, but it is worth a shot. Flipping the shot may have been interesting too.    There really is not a lot I can say about a perfect picture that just needs one thing sorting.  I love how the smooth curves all compliment each other, the red is very sensual, I could stare at lava lamps for hours.  ', '2009-09-01 20:59:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5631386, 815923, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>Nice shot, an interesting shot. <br/> <br/>The greens are very vibrant here which is a nice contrast to the little darkness that peeks out. I think that this shot would have been received better if you had cropped right into the weed.  There is too much weed here and needs to be less. <br/> <br/>In post processing, boost the contrast this will give it some more depth, even playing with the neutrals in selective colours would have given you a totally different picture. <br/> <br/>You did really well for the camera not being a macro</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   Nice shot, an interesting shot.  The greens are very vibrant here which is a nice contrast to the little darkness that peeks out. I think that this shot would have been received better if you had cropped right into the weed.  There is too much weed here and needs to be less.  In post processing, boost the contrast this will give it some more depth, even playing with the neutrals in selective colours would have given you a totally different picture.  You did really well for the camera not being a macro', '2009-09-01 21:03:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5631398, 816198, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>I don''t know a lot but I can give you what I think.  It is not macro enough, and I think in your comments you even know that. Now if there was something huge like a tiny section of the bark (walnut trees are smooth bark though) then that would have given the viewer an idea as to how small these things actually are. <br/> <br/>My eye is searching for one focal point, and i am getting three of them, one south, one west and one north. There are also some sun bubbles that direct your eye straight to them. <br/> <br/>You are sharp in your 3 areas though which is good, the background is a little busy but there is an attempt at bokeh in there (I think).  Some contrast to give it some depth would have been helpful as it would have popped the web out<br/> <br/>I gave you a six on this shot when i voted, as I did like it<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   I don''t know a lot but I can give you what I think.  It is not macro enough, and I think in your comments you even know that. Now if there was something huge like a tiny section of the bark (walnut trees are smooth bark though) then that would have given the viewer an idea as to how small these things actually are.  My eye is searching for one focal point, and i am getting three of them, one south, one west and one north. There are also some sun bubbles that direct your eye straight to them.  You are sharp in your 3 areas though which is good, the background is a little busy but there is an attempt at bokeh in there (I think).  Some contrast to give it some depth would have been helpful as it would have popped the web out I gave you a six on this shot when i voted, as I did like it ', '2009-09-01 21:13:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5631796, 815977, 59267, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful photo!! Congratulations!!</td>', 'Very beautiful photo!! Congratulations!!', '2009-09-02 01:10:27.000000', NULL, 0),
