(5632137, 815299, 78891, '<td valign="top">Congrats Karen, you''ve done the rock proud once again!</td>', 'Congrats Karen, you''ve done the rock proud once again!', '2009-09-02 07:37:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632180, 815668, 106349, '<td valign="top">Excellent finish! I love this shot... don''t know why you don''t think it''s original! :o)</td>', 'Excellent finish! I love this shot... don''t know why you don''t think it''s original! :o)', '2009-09-02 08:20:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632220, 815977, 27481, '<td valign="top">another favorite for my colection, Irene what a great shot with so much color which is what i realy love any how. and i also enjoy reading the how tos never boreing for me, keep the great shots comming we love um</td>', 'another favorite for my colection, Irene what a great shot with so much color which is what i realy love any how. and i also enjoy reading the how tos never boreing for me, keep the great shots comming we love um', '2009-09-02 08:54:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632443, 815990, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>Cool blue shot here!<br/> <br/>my 1st impressions is that it out of focus, my eye is searching for the focal point.  I am not sure if the bubbles where moving or static, but try to focus on just one bubble next time. <br/> <br/>Your shot is coming across as a little flat, play around with the brightness and contrast in your post procession to give it some depth.  Also in selective colours play with the neutrals, you will be surprised at what a difference that could make. <br/> <br/>A good try</td>', 'Hi from the C Club Cool blue shot here! my 1st impressions is that it out of focus, my eye is searching for the focal point.  I am not sure if the bubbles where moving or static, but try to focus on just one bubble next time.  Your shot is coming across as a little flat, play around with the brightness and contrast in your post procession to give it some depth.  Also in selective colours play with the neutrals, you will be surprised at what a difference that could make.  A good try', '2009-09-02 11:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632449, 815780, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from teh C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for an in depth comment of you shot in this abstract challenge.<br/> <br/>First off, well done on your top 20 very nice score indeed.  you have a compelling image here. You are tack sharp, clarity is good.  Your angles are pleasing to the eye.<br/> <br/>I played a little with this shot and found that adjusting the contrast gives it some more interesting depth, neutrals in the selective colours brought out colours that where hidden as well. Just playing around sometimes to see what can be done with these tools makes for some amazing results and downright terrible!!<br/> <br/>You did really well on this well done</td>', 'Hi from teh C Club You asked for an in depth comment of you shot in this abstract challenge. First off, well done on your top 20 very nice score indeed.  you have a compelling image here. You are tack sharp, clarity is good.  Your angles are pleasing to the eye. I played a little with this shot and found that adjusting the contrast gives it some more interesting depth, neutrals in the selective colours brought out colours that where hidden as well. Just playing around sometimes to see what can be done with these tools makes for some amazing results and downright terrible!! You did really well on this well done', '2009-09-02 11:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632472, 815639, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>YOu asked for an in depth comment on your shot. <br/> <br/>1st impression, it is very out of focus. try moving back from the subject when you have to go macro with your lens.  you can zoom in in Photoshop to get what you are after. Some contrast to separate things would have helped as well.  Flipping the canvas so that it was on the bottom looking up would have been more pleasing the eye<br/> <br/>good try,</td>', 'Hi from the C Club YOu asked for an in depth comment on your shot.  1st impression, it is very out of focus. try moving back from the subject when you have to go macro with your lens.  you can zoom in in Photoshop to get what you are after. Some contrast to separate things would have helped as well.  Flipping the canvas so that it was on the bottom looking up would have been more pleasing the eye good try,', '2009-09-02 11:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632533, 815857, 90269, '<td valign="top">Good job - really cool - it could have gone for PINK too!</td>', 'Good job - really cool - it could have gone for PINK too!', '2009-09-02 12:06:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632935, 815232, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>I can''t believe this photo didn''t finish any better than 5.33.  I think you probably got bit by the challenge topic itself.  You definitely met the abstract portion with no problem, but you have to keep in mind the finicky nature of the walmart shopper.  What they don''t see is the definitive macro element of the challenge.  Your comment from Ja-9 goes to support this idea.  She wasn''t willing to give you the benefit of the doubt, and I suspect that most other voters probably followed that simple line of thinking.<br/> <br/>As for the image itself, I think you have a beautiful shot.  The smooth curves create a good bit of interest in this abstract.  I think it''s an excellent image and would have voted it in the 8 range if I had voted on this challenge... excellent work :)<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... I can''t believe this photo didn''t finish any better than 5.33.  I think you probably got bit by the challenge topic itself.  You definitely met the abstract portion with no problem, but you have to keep in mind the finicky nature of the walmart shopper.  What they don''t see is the definitive macro element of the challenge.  Your comment from Ja-9 goes to support this idea.  She wasn''t willing to give you the benefit of the doubt, and I suspect that most other voters probably followed that simple line of thinking. As for the image itself, I think you have a beautiful shot.  The smooth curves create a good bit of interest in this abstract.  I think it''s an excellent image and would have voted it in the 8 range if I had voted on this challenge... excellent work :)', '2009-09-02 15:57:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5632982, 815299, 34591, '<td valign="top">As always, awesome photo, and incredible creativity!</td>', 'As always, awesome photo, and incredible creativity!', '2009-09-02 16:21:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5633242, 815780, 73942, '<td valign="top">Janine - congrats on a great finish</td>', 'Janine - congrats on a great finish', '2009-09-02 20:00:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5633832, 815619, 50641, '<td valign="top">This was in my top 10 - it looks like something on the wall at MOMA. Love the way it curves up at the ends and the magnitude of saturation you achieved.  Frame is just right too.  Congrats on a personal top 5 photo!</td>', 'This was in my top 10 - it looks like something on the wall at MOMA. Love the way it curves up at the ends and the magnitude of saturation you achieved.  Frame is just right too.  Congrats on a personal top 5 photo!', '2009-09-03 01:24:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634251, 815762, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for an in depth comment on your shot.<br/> <br/>Brilliant idea!! Very colourful!<br/> <br/>Now lets do some nitty gritty stuff.  First off it does look like it is out of focus, i see that was touched upon by your comments as well. On your original shot, that is definitely soft, not so much out of focus , but soft <br/> <br/>Looking at it for a fairly long time, you can see where your focus was when you shot this.  I think what is happening here is more along the lines of an optical illusion.  Your focus is on about 3 pieces of glass, the rest is soft, because there is so much glass, it over whelms the in focus pieces. This one was a very difficult shot to get in focus and look like it was in focus. <br/> <br/>The lighting is fairly harsh on this as well, have  you thought about sticking a light bulb into the glass?  You said that you are trying different things, there are tons of different ways to light something as well.<br/> <br/>Going from the original shot to this, I see that you did use sharpening and you did it really well. There is not a lot more you could do in post processing that would have made a huge difference as your saturations and colours are good. <br/> <br/>And you don''t suck, you are learning, we are all learning and growing, just as you are!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club You asked for an in depth comment on your shot. Brilliant idea!! Very colourful! Now lets do some nitty gritty stuff.  First off it does look like it is out of focus, i see that was touched upon by your comments as well. On your original shot, that is definitely soft, not so much out of focus , but soft  Looking at it for a fairly long time, you can see where your focus was when you shot this.  I think what is happening here is more along the lines of an optical illusion.  Your focus is on about 3 pieces of glass, the rest is soft, because there is so much glass, it over whelms the in focus pieces. This one was a very difficult shot to get in focus and look like it was in focus.  The lighting is fairly harsh on this as well, have  you thought about sticking a light bulb into the glass?  You said that you are trying different things, there are tons of different ways to light something as well. Going from the original shot to this, I see that you did use sharpening and you did it really well. There is not a lot more you could do in post processing that would have made a huge difference as your saturations and colours are good.  And you don''t suck, you are learning, we are all learning and growing, just as you are! ', '2009-09-03 10:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634267, 815290, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>I really like the simplicity of this shot, very nice to see.<br/> <br/>You did very well on the saturations of colours, the colours themselves, the DOF and the POV.  I think what is hurting this though is the blur that you have going on in the front of the shot.  Cropping it right up to the in focus dribbles would have been more pleasing to the eye. <br/> <br/>Your sharpness is tack sharp, this is a very good shot and one i can see hanging on a wall, well done</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   I really like the simplicity of this shot, very nice to see. You did very well on the saturations of colours, the colours themselves, the DOF and the POV.  I think what is hurting this though is the blur that you have going on in the front of the shot.  Cropping it right up to the in focus dribbles would have been more pleasing to the eye.  Your sharpness is tack sharp, this is a very good shot and one i can see hanging on a wall, well done', '2009-09-03 10:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634276, 816183, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>A cool blue shot here and definitely a macro, well done. <br/> <br/>I think with this shot, to make it a more powerful one, would be to flip it on end and have a little more black space. <br/> <br/>In post processing, some contrast would have separated the bristles some, your colour is pure blue, maybe playing a little with the neutral/black colours in selective colours, would have given you more contrast as well, very nicely done.  You are tack sharp, your DOF is excellent. <br/> <br/>Good shot<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   A cool blue shot here and definitely a macro, well done.  I think with this shot, to make it a more powerful one, would be to flip it on end and have a little more black space.  In post processing, some contrast would have separated the bristles some, your colour is pure blue, maybe playing a little with the neutral/black colours in selective colours, would have given you more contrast as well, very nicely done.  You are tack sharp, your DOF is excellent.  Good shot ', '2009-09-03 11:03:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634310, 816141, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>Super cool shot, i really like it. <br/> <br/>There is not a lot to critique on this shot, you have good colours, i like how the background black has a tint of green in it as well. Your gold green, is spot on, your bubble is tack tack sharp, rule of thirds is good, your POV and DOF is spot on. <br/> <br/>My own personal nitpick is the end of your interesting shot is out of focus, that is it.  <br/> <br/>Good shot</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   Super cool shot, i really like it.  There is not a lot to critique on this shot, you have good colours, i like how the background black has a tint of green in it as well. Your gold green, is spot on, your bubble is tack tack sharp, rule of thirds is good, your POV and DOF is spot on.  My own personal nitpick is the end of your interesting shot is out of focus, that is it.   Good shot', '2009-09-03 11:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634774, 816252, 30982, '<td valign="top">Woefully underappreciated.  This is really quite good in my opinion.</td>', 'Woefully underappreciated.  This is really quite good in my opinion.', '2009-09-03 17:51:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634939, 816249, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club, <br/> <br/>You certainly have a macro going on here!!!<br/> <br/>This is excellent macro, you are sharp, clean cut, your DOF is excellent and POV is interesting. I belive that the reason this did not score highly was because it is a pretty boring photograph. <br/> <br/>But in saying that, you have mastered on how to do a macro, you have sharpness that is tack sharp your leading line is excellent, your colours are spot on. <br/> <br/>You have done really well with this, and you have got this macro down, now lets find some interesting subjects!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club,  You certainly have a macro going on here!!! This is excellent macro, you are sharp, clean cut, your DOF is excellent and POV is interesting. I belive that the reason this did not score highly was because it is a pretty boring photograph.  But in saying that, you have mastered on how to do a macro, you have sharpness that is tack sharp your leading line is excellent, your colours are spot on.  You have done really well with this, and you have got this macro down, now lets find some interesting subjects! ', '2009-09-03 20:06:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635036, 816099, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Pretty colours, and I never would have guessed that it was part if a fireplug!<br/> <br/>Technical: DOF is good, lighting good.  My eye is doing a lot of roving around looking for a focal point. As has been noted there is a lot to look at here.  In this challenge, it works well because you want to keep the viewer guessing, but don''t use this as a fallback.<br/>Wondering why such a fast shutter speed?  A slower shutter, even handheld (see no mention of use of a tripod) could have given you a shot with much more depth and texture, and less reliance on pp tricks.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Favourable comments from viewers and a respectable score, who''s to argue with that?<br/> <br/>Overall: A little too much for me personally in terms of pp, but it did well and it is nice to see the thumb of the hydrant and area you macro''d in on.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Pretty colours, and I never would have guessed that it was part if a fireplug! Technical: DOF is good, lighting good.  My eye is doing a lot of roving around looking for a focal point. As has been noted there is a lot to look at here.  In this challenge, it works well because you want to keep the viewer guessing, but don''t use this as a fallback.Wondering why such a fast shutter speed?  A slower shutter, even handheld (see no mention of use of a tripod) could have given you a shot with much more depth and texture, and less reliance on pp tricks. Artistic: Favourable comments from viewers and a respectable score, who''s to argue with that? Overall: A little too much for me personally in terms of pp, but it did well and it is nice to see the thumb of the hydrant and area you macro''d in on. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-09-03 21:56:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635043, 815979, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Oh yeah, I''ve see those around here too, nice capture.  <br/> <br/>Technical: Composition plays safe in that it is very centred.  Light and dof good.  Colours are vibrant and attractive.  I agree that a different crop may have helped give more of an abstract feel to shot.<br/> <br/>Artistic: I like the near-zoomblur effect here to the heart of the pistil.  Like the green leaf(?) in top left corner that helps break up the centredness and draws the eye away a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: Not the most exciting shot in the challenge, it is quite apparent what it is.  But your treatment of it makes it more interesting.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Oh yeah, I''ve see those around here too, nice capture.   Technical: Composition plays safe in that it is very centred.  Light and dof good.  Colours are vibrant and attractive.  I agree that a different crop may have helped give more of an abstract feel to shot. Artistic: I like the near-zoomblur effect here to the heart of the pistil.  Like the green leaf(?) in top left corner that helps break up the centredness and draws the eye away a little. Overall: Not the most exciting shot in the challenge, it is quite apparent what it is.  But your treatment of it makes it more interesting. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-09-03 22:02:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635694, 816177, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from teh C Club<br/> <br/>you asked for an indepth comment on your shot in this challenge. <br/> <br/>It is an excellent macro and great abstract.  I don''t think anyone could have guessed what this was.  You have an excellent bokeh going on here. Would have been nice to see a little more of the glass/stem? as this has gorgeous flowing lines and gives it a focal point. <br/> <br/>I can see nothing that would add to this in post processing<br/> <br/></td>', 'HI from teh C Club you asked for an indepth comment on your shot in this challenge.  It is an excellent macro and great abstract.  I don''t think anyone could have guessed what this was.  You have an excellent bokeh going on here. Would have been nice to see a little more of the glass/stem? as this has gorgeous flowing lines and gives it a focal point.  I can see nothing that would add to this in post processing ', '2009-09-04 11:48:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635714, 816060, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>you asked for an indepth comment of you shot for this challenge<br/> <br/>first off, nice shot, you have got this macro down pat, well done.  As for the abstract part, not so much. IF you had zoomed in on say the screw and the teeth of it, then it would be more abstract but still holding definition. <br/> <br/>your focal point is good and your DOF and POV is excellent. In post processing though, play around with the blacks, selective colours and shadow and highlights, then convert it to black and white as this is coming across as fairly flat. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club you asked for an indepth comment of you shot for this challenge first off, nice shot, you have got this macro down pat, well done.  As for the abstract part, not so much. IF you had zoomed in on say the screw and the teeth of it, then it would be more abstract but still holding definition.  your focal point is good and your DOF and POV is excellent. In post processing though, play around with the blacks, selective colours and shadow and highlights, then convert it to black and white as this is coming across as fairly flat.  ', '2009-09-04 11:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635721, 816025, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>you asked for an in depth comment on your shot in this challenge. <br/> <br/>First off, looking at your placement, i am very surprised and also surprised at the low score.  I thought this was one of the most interesting shot in this challenge. <br/> <br/>I think what is hurting this shot is the fact that it is not very abstract.  It is an abstract shot, but for some reason most people think of unrecognizable things when they think abstract. <br/> <br/>Your post processing is spot on, there is nothing that i can see that i think would improve this shot/  IT is tack sharp, saturations and colours are excellent, good POV and the DOF is very good. <br/> <br/>If this had been in the macro challenge I could see it winning a ribbon.</td>', 'Hi from the C Club you asked for an in depth comment on your shot in this challenge.  First off, looking at your placement, i am very surprised and also surprised at the low score.  I thought this was one of the most interesting shot in this challenge.  I think what is hurting this shot is the fact that it is not very abstract.  It is an abstract shot, but for some reason most people think of unrecognizable things when they think abstract.  Your post processing is spot on, there is nothing that i can see that i think would improve this shot/  IT is tack sharp, saturations and colours are excellent, good POV and the DOF is very good.  If this had been in the macro challenge I could see it winning a ribbon.', '2009-09-04 12:01:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635732, 816144, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from teh C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for an in dpeth comment on your shot in this challenge. <br/> <br/>First off, I am not sure whether to say eww or wowwwwwww.  This is an excellent image of making the imagination soar.  It is a very powerful image.  We know what it is, but our minds take over as to what it could be, what a powerful thing you have done to us all. <br/> <br/>I think that taking the stem off would have given this a more abstract feeling.  Abstracts are a weird thing really.  Some people think they should just be a blurry odd unrecognized thing and then others think that you should be able to identify it. <br/> <br/>I can see nothing that would improve this shot or any suggestions. <br/> <br/>Well done on this</td>', 'Hi from teh C Club You asked for an in dpeth comment on your shot in this challenge.  First off, I am not sure whether to say eww or wowwwwwww.  This is an excellent image of making the imagination soar.  It is a very powerful image.  We know what it is, but our minds take over as to what it could be, what a powerful thing you have done to us all.  I think that taking the stem off would have given this a more abstract feeling.  Abstracts are a weird thing really.  Some people think they should just be a blurry odd unrecognized thing and then others think that you should be able to identify it.  I can see nothing that would improve this shot or any suggestions.  Well done on this', '2009-09-04 12:08:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5635797, 816144, 109903, '<td valign="top">i think this is a great pic. surprised at the ratings, though. it has such great texture and clarity that it should have gotten at least some 10s!</td>', 'i think this is a great pic. surprised at the ratings, though. it has such great texture and clarity that it should have gotten at least some 10s!', '2009-09-04 12:36:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5637491, 816252, 40370, '<td valign="top">Voted 9, I loved this one. So much more abstract than a bug. It made me think for a minute, recognizable ... ultimately ... okay, but so are bubbles in oil. The Blue win in "rule of thirds" helps ease the pain, I would imagine. Nice going in both instances.</td>', 'Voted 9, I loved this one. So much more abstract than a bug. It made me think for a minute, recognizable ... ultimately ... okay, but so are bubbles in oil. The Blue win in "rule of thirds" helps ease the pain, I would imagine. Nice going in both instances.', '2009-09-05 22:41:51.000000', NULL, 0),
